  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"assets/icon.svg\" width=\"88\" alt=\"\"></p>\n\n<h1 align=\"center\">dsh-jiuwen-adapter</h1>\n\n<p align=\"center\"><b>Use JiuwenSwarm as the brain of dsh, with your other dsh plugins still working.</b></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/ThinkFlowLab/dsh-jiuwen-adapter/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/ThinkFlowLab/dsh-jiuwen-adapter/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg?branch=main\" alt=\"CI\"></a>\n  <a href=\"./docs/testing.md\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/tests-guarded-22c55e\" alt=\"tests guarded\"></a>\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/package-json/v/ThinkFlowLab/dsh-jiuwen-adapter?label=version\" alt=\"version\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/dsh-%3E%3D0.2.1--rc.2%20%3C0.3.0-6366f1\" alt=\"dsh range\">\n  <a href=\"./LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache--2.0-blue\" alt=\"license\"></a>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"./README.zh.md\">中文</a> · <a href=\"./docs/quickstart.md\">Quickstart</a> · <a href=\"./docs/configuration.md\">Config</a> · <a href=\"./docs/dsh-integration.md\">dsh integration</a> · <a href=\"./CHANGELOG.md\">Changelog</a></p>\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "A Cordis plugin that registers a `jiuwen` provider on `ctx.llm`. dsh still handles the UI, sessions, approvals and plugins. Each turn goes to the [JiuwenSwarm](https://pypi.org/project/workswarm/) Gateway, which runs its own agents, tools and memory.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  D[\"dsh + your plugins\"] -->|ctx.llm · provider=jiuwen| A[\"jiuwen adapter\"] -->|\"WS chat.send\"| G[\"JiuwenSwarm Gateway :19000\"]\n```\n\n- Plugin compatibility: [docs/plugin-compat.md](docs/plugin-compat.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "30-second quickstart",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Brain: start JiuwenSwarm (put your model key in ~/.jiuwenswarm/config/.env)",
      "text": "uv pip install workswarm && jiuwenswarm-init && jiuwenswarm-start app"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Plugin: install into a dsh profile (dsh >= 0.2.1-rc.2: npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@next)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add \"git+https://github.com/ThinkFlowLab/dsh-jiuwen-adapter.git\""
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Make it the default model, then chat",
      "text": "printf -- '- id: agent-default-model\\n  config:\\n    provider: jiuwen\\n    model: jiuwen-default\\n' >> ~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml\ndsh --profile web\n```\n\nStep-by-step guide for Mac and Linux: **[docs/quickstart.md](./docs/quickstart.md)**. To try it without a Gateway, run `npm run mock:gateway`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "| | What you get | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🧠 **Jiuwen brain** | One dsh turn is one Gateway `chat.send`. Agents, team mode, skills and memory run in Jiuwen | on |\n| 💬 **Live activity** | Reasoning, 🔧 tool calls, subtasks and token usage stream into dsh | on |\n| ✅ **dsh approvals and questions** | Jiuwen permission prompts, plan approval and `ask_user` go through dsh's own dialogs, and deny when no answer comes | on |\n| 🔁 **Session continuity** | dsh sessions map to Jiuwen sessions. Only new text is sent after the first turn | on |\n| 🛟 **Drop recovery** | If the Gateway drops mid-answer, the reply is recovered from history and marked as recovered | on |\n| 🧾 **Local titles and compaction** | Titles and `/compact` are handled locally, so they never cost a Jiuwen turn | on |\n| ⌨️ **`/jiuwen` command** | Sessions, models, modes, skills, agents, cron, MCP and more ([list](./docs/dsh-integration.md#5-jiuwen-slash-command-dsh-command-registry)) | on |\n| 🖼️ **Multimodal** | Image and file parts are sent as Jiuwen media | on |\n| 🪪 **System prompt → Jiuwen** | `injectSystem: full\\|persona` sends the host system prompt (any role/profile) once per Jiuwen session, resent only on change, capped"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Other dsh plugins must keep working. The adapter is tested against the **full dsh agent runtime** (`dsh-agent`, `dsh-agent-loop`, compaction, subagents, goals, plan mode, a bash sandbox, approvals and user-questions). The same scripted session runs once with jiuwen loaded and once without. Every row of the [compat matrix](./docs/known-issues.md#15-round-8-full-runtime-scenarios--version-matrix) must match, covering events, tool calls, plan exit, goal rounds, auto-compaction, subagents, bash, host event counts, globals and load failures."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Component | Supported | Tested in CI |\n|---|---|---|\n| dsh | `>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0` | 0.2.1-rc.2, 0.2.1-rc.5 |\n| Cordis | `^4.0.5` | 4.0.5 |\n| Node | `>=22` | 22, 24 |\n| JiuwenSwarm | 0.2.x Gateway | 0.2.7 (live) |\n\nThe adapter also works in any Cordis app that has an `llm` service ([usage](./docs/usage.md))."
    },
    {
      "section": "Docs",
      "text": "- [Quickstart](./docs/quickstart.md), [Configuration](./docs/configuration.md), [Troubleshooting](./docs/troubleshooting.md)\n- [Using it from code and Gateway features](./docs/usage.md), [Gateway RPC coverage](./docs/coverage.md)\n- [dsh integration](./docs/dsh-integration.md), [Host → Jiuwen sync](./docs/host-sync.md), [Testing](./docs/testing.md), [Known issues and test logs](./docs/known-issues.md)\n- [Publishing to a dsh plugin market](./docs/marketplace.md), [Architecture](./ARCHITECTURE.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm run lint                  # node --check over index.js, src/, bin/, scripts/, test/\nnpm test                      # unit, mock-gateway and runtime suites\nnpm run test:coverage         # + coverage floors and the test-count baseline (what CI runs)\nbash scripts/guard-live.sh    # box-side nightly live guard (real Jiuwen + plain dsh), see docs/testing.md\n\nLicensed under [Apache-2.0](./LICENSE)."
    }
  ],
